**Files (5 shared single-writer):**
- `rust/crates/host/src/router.rs` — the six support routes after the
  attendance mount.
- `rust/crates/pg-fixture/src/lib.rs` — `SUPPORT_MIGRATIONS`, the
  `support_ledger` field, the nineteenth provision step (after attendance),
  its runtime grants, the `migrations_package` and `ledger_expectations`
  arms, and both constructors.
- `tools/rust/verify.mjs` — the R07 fast-gate comment + the twelve support
  check mappings.
- `tools/rust/test/verify.test.mjs` — the R07 witness-map suite allowlist
  (support) and the frozen `witnessTotal` comment (40 → 52).
- `docs/rust/required-coverage.json` — `P-ERP-R07` grows to 52 checks,
  `witnessTotal` 52, the support `sourcePaths` and the producedBy clause.

**What the cohort is.** Twelve commands (`case.create`, `case.start`,
`case.wait`, `case.resume`, `case.close`, `case.cancel`, `case.resolve`,
`case.reopen`, `case.assign`, `case.set-priority`, `case.set-target`,
`note.add`) against `archava_support`'s six tables. Every command lands one
command row, one audit row, one transition row (where the arm moves the
case) and a receipt; the deferred `case_complete` trigger refuses any commit
whose audit count ≠ case revision or whose last transition/receipt disagree,
so a partial history cannot exist. `case.create` writes revision 1 and does
not take the common UPDATE; every later arm takes an optimistic revision
check. A duplicate `(tenant, requestId)` replays its stored receipt, a
changed payload conflicts (409), a stale revision conflicts, and the state
table refuses illegal moves. Notes are append-only and separately gated
(`notes.write` / `cases.read`); the audit read is its own grant. The
assignee picker is tenant-wide, active-human-only, bounded and returns
`cases.read` holders; assignment requires `cases.assign` AND
`scope=all` AND an active human with `cases.read`. Four read projections
(access, assignees, case worklist, case detail+history) narrow on
`scope=assigned` exactly like the TS api. Twelve named witnesses grow the
same `P-ERP-R07` proof from 40 to 52; the support schema's complete-history
trigger is the deferred condition the host maps to the 409 conflict carrier
at commit.

**Apply:** `patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 < PACKET-010.diff` on
main+004…009. The new source files
(`domain|adapters|host/src/erp/support.rs`, `host/tests/erp_support.rs`, the
three `mod.rs` lines, `tools/rust/erp/verify-r07.mjs`, `packages/support-pg/`
and the `docs/rust/archxy2/` reports) are delivered by the candidate copy.
